      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e can we call this just \u0027apexlist\u0027?\n\nMy first idea was \"flattenedApexList\", but for now it became the list of APEXes which are \"installable \u0026\u0026 device\". What about \"deviceInstalledApexList\"?\n\n\u003e I still think special casing the vndk APEX case is the right approach.\n\nI can\u0027t call it \u0027right\u0027 because of reasons I mentioned in commit message. Sepolicy for flattened apexes may break due to apex_name and file_contexts properties.\n\nBy the way, I\u0027d separate this stuff from the change because it is somewhat different topic. And I think there are more to do with sepolicy for flattened apexes when they are installed other than system partition.",
      "parentUuid": "50cbab65_00163b7c",
